using HyperWhisper.ModelManagement;
using HyperWhisper.ModelReadiness;

namespace HyperWhisper.PortableApplication;

/// <summary>A model's (speed, accuracy) pair, each 1-5, as the Model Library gauges draw it.</summary>
public readonly record struct ModelRating(int Speed, int Accuracy);

/// <summary>
/// The empirical speed/accuracy ratings behind the Model Library's "Speed / Accuracy" column,
/// sourced from the macOS benchmark in <c>benchmarks/</c> (regenerated by
/// <c>benchmarks/propose_ratings.py</c> and <c>benchmarks/propose_pp_ratings.py</c>).
///
/// This is the SHARED copy. Two hand-maintained copies of these numbers already existed, in
/// app/windows/HyperWhisper/Services/ModelLibraryManager.cs (lines ~446-559) and in
/// app/macos/hyperwhisper/Managers/ModelLibraryManager.swift, and the Linux head had no copy at
/// all, which is why its third column showed a readiness word where the other two draw meters.
/// The tables live here now so a rating is edited in one place. The Windows head still compiles
/// its own private dictionaries: this branch is not allowed to edit app/windows, so deleting
/// them and pointing ModelLibraryManager at this type is the follow-up, and until that lands
/// ModelRatingsParityTests pins the two sets equal by parsing the Windows source. Do not "fix" a
/// number here alone; change it here and let that test tell you what else to update.
///
/// FOUR tables, not one, and the split is load-bearing: six ids appear in both
/// <see cref="Cloud"/> and <see cref="PostProcessing"/> with DIFFERENT values (gemini-2.5-flash,
/// gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3-flash-preview, gemini-3.1-pro-preview,
/// gemini-3.1-flash-lite), because a model that transcribes well does not necessarily clean text
/// up well. Merging the dictionaries would silently corrupt all six.
/// </summary>
public static class ModelRatings
{
    /// <summary>The rating an unmeasured model gets: "average, unmeasured".</summary>
    public static readonly ModelRating Default = new(3, 3);

    /// <summary>
    /// Parakeet's fallback is deliberately NOT <see cref="Default"/>. Every model on this
    /// runtime is a fast transducer, so an unmeasured one is far likelier to be a 5 for speed
    /// than a 3. Mirrors ModelLibraryManager.cs:132.
    /// </summary>
    public static readonly ModelRating ParakeetDefault = new(5, 3);

